{{!
    @template enrol_apply/report_view

    The course report's React view (stage R4, Moodle 5.3 only): one mount point, core's own
    rendering of the report for a browser without JavaScript, and the way to core's table.

    The mount names the bundle (js/esm/bundle.json): one ES module built from
    js/esm/src/report/ReportView.tsx, so the client arrives in one request. Its inner content is
    what the first paint shows until React commits, which replaces it: a skeleton in the shape of
    the band and the grid, and, hidden behind it, one sentence that is true only if the component
    never mounts. styles.css swaps the two about 10 s after the first paint, so no pulse lasts for
    ever. Both are shown only under body.jsenabled; only the mounted component draws rows, so a
    step asserting an applicant's name in the view asserts that React ran.

    The props arrive already JSON-encoded by enrol_apply\output\report_view, in one value, through
    a triple stash: nothing between here and React is an HTML context. They carry configuration and
    strings, never a row.

    The noscript holds core's rendering of the report without its filter form; the link under it
    is core's table with JavaScript, which keeps every filter core offers.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * props - the component's props, JSON.
    * tableurl - report.php with view=table.
    * noscript - core's rendering of the report, HTML.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "props": "{\"enrolid\": 3, \"labels\": {\"loading\": \"Loading applications\"}, \"perpage\": 30}",
        "tableurl": "https://example.com/enrol/apply/report.php?id=3&view=table",
        "noscript": "<p>Core's report</p>"
    }
}}
<div class="enrol_apply-rview" data-enrol-apply-report="view">
    <p class="enrol_apply-rview-tablelink">
        <a href="{{tableurl}}">{{#str}}reportviewtableview, enrol_apply{{/str}}</a>
    </p>
    {{#react}}
    {
        "component": "@moodle/lms/enrol_apply/bundle",
        "props": {{{props}}},
        "class": "enrol_apply-rview-mount"
    }
    <div class="enrol_apply-rview-preload" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="enrol_apply-rview-band">
            <div class="enrol_apply-rview-tile enrol_apply-rview-sk"><span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb"></span><span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb enrol_apply-rview-skb--big"></span></div>
            <div class="enrol_apply-rview-tile enrol_apply-rview-sk"><span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb"></span><span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb enrol_apply-rview-skb--big"></span></div>
            <div class="enrol_apply-rview-tile enrol_apply-rview-sk"><span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb"></span><span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb enrol_apply-rview-skb--big"></span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="enrol_apply-rview-skgrid enrol_apply-rview-sk">
            <span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb"></span>
            <span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb"></span>
            <span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb"></span>
            <span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb"></span>
            <span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb"></span>
        </div>
    </div>
    <p class="enrol_apply-rview-failed">{{#str}}reportviewmountfailed, enrol_apply{{/str}}</p>
    {{/react}}
    <noscript>{{{noscript}}}</noscript>
</div>
